         <section anchor="congestion-on-the-ack-path" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-6.1.4">
           <name slugifiedName="name-congestion-on-the-ack-path">Congestion on the ACK-path</name>
-          <t indent="0" pn="section-6.1.4-1">For the current generation of TCP congestion control algorithms, pure
-acknowledgement packets (e.g., packets that do not contain any
-accompanying data) should be sent with the ECT bit off. Current TCP
-receivers have no mechanisms for reducing traffic on the ACK-path in
